Title: GREYHARBOR
Episode: 104 "Hush Money"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - MORNING

The police tape hangs loose. Mara stands inside anyway, comparing the fake harbor book to pages she copied from the leather ledger.

Lila slips in with a stack of tide permits.

LILA
Cole asked me to tell him if you came here.

MARA
And you did?

LILA
I told the wall. It listens better.

Mara points to a column of initials.

MARA
C.B. paid Tobias every Thursday, then paid him double the week Danny vanished.

LILA
Deputies don't make double anything.

EXT. COUNTY ROAD - DAY

Mara walks the shoulder. Gideon's truck crawls beside her, window down.

GIDEON
You know walking makes people wonder what you stole.

MARA
Let them wonder.

MARA
The ledger names a boat called the Black Osprey. I find that boat, I find who bought Cole.

GIDEON
Never heard of it.

MARA
That was almost convincing.

INT. EDDA'S KITCHEN - DAY

Edda chops onions one-handed. Her right hand is wrapped in a white burn dressing.

MARA
You need the clinic.

EDDA
Clinic asks names.

MARA
You can't use your right hand.

EDDA
Then the left one gets promoted.

EXT. OLD CANNERY - DUSK

Cole meets Rafi under broken loading cranes. Rafi hands him the radio note.

COLE
Nerida Glass.

RAFI
You know her?

COLE
I know what happens to men who say her name twice.

RAFI
The buoy's gone. The south channel is blind.

COLE
Good. Blind things obey.

INT. SALT HOUSE COLD ROOM - NIGHT

Mara and Danny enter a refrigerated room whose motor no longer runs. Frost has become sweat on the walls.

Danny pries open a drain grate. Inside: a roll of wet film, tied in oilcloth.

DANNY
Tobias said if I ever got cornered, the cold room owed me one favor.

MARA
He knew you were alive.

DANNY
He knew I was scared.

EXT. SALT HOUSE - NIGHT

Cole watches from the lane as Mara and Danny slip away.

He strikes a match and drops it into a trail of lamp oil.

The Salt House cold room flashes white behind the windows. The roof folds inward. The cold room is gone.

INT. FERRY OFFICE - NIGHT

Gideon threads the wet film through a hand viewer. Mara watches images stutter across the wall: Tobias arguing with Cole outside the chapel.

MARA
Cole shot him.

GIDEON
Film doesn't say who pulled the trigger.

MARA
Tobias's face does.

EXT. BREAKWATER - NIGHT

Cole backs toward the surf with Mara, Danny, and Gideon spread out before him.

COLE
You don't know what that ledger bought.

MARA
My uncle's grave?

COLE
Your brother's life.

Danny steps forward. Cole reaches for his gun.

A shot cracks from the dark. Cole drops hard against the stones. His hat rolls into the wash.

Mara kneels. Cole's eyes are open and empty.

DANNY
Who fired?

No one answers.

FADE OUT.
